{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790180281,"nonce":"vnXjIm28X6EA8SCFFCWpUQ3BnmI=","title":"Decided 2026-09-23 with Luis.","message":"1. The entity keeps the name `issue` (refs/work-issues, `git work issue`, entities/issue). Considered `item` / work-items now that the entity also holds iterations and initiatives, and now was the only cheap moment (all of it uncommitted). Kept `issue` because it is the word Jira, Linear and GitHub use and Jira is canonical; Jira's own issue types include Initiative and Epic, so only iterations stretch it, and plumbing is agent-facing (people type `git work flow sprint new`); and `item` collides with vocabulary already in the code (AddValue items, config SetItem, Snapshot.Items). A `git work item` CLI alias later costs one line if wanted.\n\n2. Every field and relation config entity belongs to exactly one issue type: identity is (kind, type, key), all fixed at Create. `status` on task and `status` on epic are two entities with the same key and possibly different values; the issue stores `status` and the engine resolves the entity by the issue's type. This is Jira's model (field configurations and workflows per issue type), so the sync instantiates per type instead of inferring what is shared. Consequences: the `types` applicability attribute on fields is gone; per-type value sets need no special case; `parent` on each type carries its own target_types, so the allowed_parents item set on type entities is gone and target_types is the one constraint; duplicate resolution (E7) keys on (kind, type, key); reconcile matches by (kind, type, key); the schema YAML is type-first. Sharing is an authoring concern: YAML anchors in the schema file, one definition reconciling into one entity per type; a `template` kind can come later if anchors are not enough. Built-ins stay in code and apply to every type; a per-type entity with a built-in key overrides its configurable parts. Cost accepted: renaming a status across five types is five operations, which is what `schema import` is for.","files":null}]}